photograph-eyebrow = THE PHOTOGRAPH ON THE WEST WALL
photograph-title = A platform beside the sea
photograph-copy = Two people. One suitcase.
    Back then, you thought every departure
    would bring you home together.
photograph-caption = Summer 1947 · The seaside platform
    On the back, a date you wrote together.
letter-eyebrow = INSIDE THE SAFE · AN UNSENT LETTER
letter-title = All those nights with the lamp on
letter-copy = I thought that if I left the lamp on,
    you would know I was waiting.

    Later I learned that love could also mean
    wishing you well somewhere else.

    Take the key. You need not keep
    that summer safe for me any longer.
letter-caption = M.
letter-take = Keep the letter and take the key ↗
